    "datasource": "Kodak Kodachrome 25, 64 and 200 Professional Film, publication E-55, June 2009 (page 5); SHA256 89ef8788a2a830e84e342d9f6f200336f31b0327adbc4ae5396517b3cfc0d2aa. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/kodak-kodachrome200/recipe.json. Dye spectra: this sheet, rescaled against its own visual neutral. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Not on the sheet; the dye panel is normalised and plots no D-min. A flat 0.10 is assumed, within the range the shipped positives carry. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from kodak_kodachrome_64. Nearest shipped sibling: the same process K-14 reversal family, from the same datasheet. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [1.0849, 0.9653, 0.8688], log-exposure shift [-0.001, 0.0, -0.0026], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 37.3% before, 9.2% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
